full-query: "You are designing a hybrid cloud architecture with Google Cloud and your on-premises network. Your organization has a Dedicated Interconnect connection between your on-premises network and a Google Cloud region (Region A). You also have a Bare Metal Solution for Oracle set up in Region B. You need to configure the networking so that a Compute Engine instance in Region A can connect to the Oracle database on the Bare Metal Solution machine in Region B. What should you do?"
